111342.153: [11:13:42]# 
111342.153: [11:13:42]# To define the time you can provide concrete values for
111342.153: [11:13:42]# minute (m), hour (h), day of month (dom), month (mon),
111342.153: [11:13:42]# and day of week (dow) or use '*' in these fields (for 'any').
111342.153: [11:13:42]# 
111342.153: [11:13:42]# Notice that tasks will be started based on the cron's system
111342.153: [11:13:42]# daemon's notion of time and timezones.
111342.153: [11:13:42]# 
111342.153: [11:13:42]# Output of the crontab jobs (including errors) is sent through
111342.153: [11:13:42]# email to the user the crontab file belongs to (unless redirected).
111342.153: [11:13:42]# 
